      "short": "rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/5N2/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKB1R 1. Nf3 is the third most popular initial move. It is highly flexible and often transposes…",
      "wikibookUrl": "https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Chess_Opening_Theory/1._Nf3",
      "wikibookExcerpt": "rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/5N2/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKB1R 1. Nf3 is the third most popular initial move. It is highly flexible and often transposes into lines better known through other move orders, though some independent lines are possible. White reckons that Nf3 will almost certainly be a useful move sooner or later, whereas every pawn move is an irrevocable commitment, so 1. Nf3 keeps White's options open.",
