      "wikibookExcerpt": "This opening is a hypermodern opening, which invites white's minor pieces to control the centre rather than their pawns. Here black has 4 options: This can be done with moves such as 2... c6, or 2... e6, both of which generally transpose to the Queen's Gambit Declined or Slav Defense. However, white can deviate with 3. g3, leading the positions that resemble the Catalan Opening (or even transposing to the Catalan Opening, normally reached with 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3), or even 3. b3!?",
